{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>For</b> — Some say: <b>יתחמץ</b> is from the root of <b>חומץ</b> (vinegar) by way of parable, for my heart turns to vinegar within my kidneys, when I ponder [it], from the root <b>חץ</b> [in the sense of] sharpened. And R. Moses interpreted it: in the language of our Sages of blessed memory, <b>חמץ את הדין</b> (he fermented/sharpened the judgment)."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 73, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:18.341504720Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}